# This file lives in cli/ on purpose: cli/ is subtree-pushed to the public GitHub mirror, so
# these rules travel with it. The monorepo's root .gitignore does NOT reach the mirror.
#
# .npmrc is the one that matters. It is where an npm token goes
# (//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=...), and without a rule for it a token file created here
# shows up as an ordinary untracked file that `git add -A` will happily stage — into a repo
# that is published. Root .gitignore covers node_modules and *.tgz for cli/, but not this.
.npmrc
.env.npm-token
.env.local

# Also covered by the root .gitignore for the monorepo; repeated here so the mirror stands alone.
node_modules/
*.tgz
